        },
        "title": "Description and rationale",
        "body": "One authored operation in a repeatable workflow, with inputs, outputs, success route, failure policy, and authority boundary.\n\nClass key: `workflow-step`. Instances hold their authored fields in node.data and render through this class's faces. Edges connect using named ports; no data JSON blob substitutes for a class.\n\nOrdering is read from `workflow.next` edges between named `next` and `previous` ports. It is not duplicated in a text field.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
